<launch>
  <!-- EPIC <- FAST-LIVO2 (LIO-only), Livox Mid-360.

       Grounded in the prior code (not guessed):
       * FAST-LIVO2 LIVMapper.cpp:1338-1352 — odom header.frame_id="camera_init",
         child="aft_mapped"; it BROADCASTS tf camera_init->aft_mapped itself;
         /cloud_registered is also in camera_init. It only publishes
         /aft_mapped_to_init (there is no /aft_mapped_to_odom).
       * EPIC lidar_map_interface.cpp:126 — map_frame is taken FROM the odom
         message header (adopts camera_init); sim_lio.cpp:67 — cloud_frame ==
         map_frame => identity, no tf lookup.
       => For LIO-only NO custom TF bridge is needed. The README's
          smart_static_tf_bridge.py was camera_link->camera_init (camera path
          only), irrelevant without the D455.

       The ONLY wiring change vs EPIC's own d455.launch is the odom topic
       name: EPIC subscribes /aft_mapped_to_odom (config/d455.yaml) but
       FAST-LIVO2 publishes /aft_mapped_to_init. A top-level <remap> before
       the <include> rewrites it for every node in d455.launch. We do NOT
       edit the gitignored EPIC clone; this wrapper lives in the tracked
       stack repo.

       Run inside dps-dev, shared master :11399, with the Mid-360 driver +
       FAST-LIVO2 (slam_planning/fastlivo/mapping_mid360_lio.launch) already up:
         export ROS_MASTER_URI=http://localhost:11399
         source /work/ros_ws/devel/setup.bash
         roslaunch /work/slam_planning/epic/epic_mid360_lio.launch
       Trigger exploration (frame MUST be camera_init):
         rostopic pub -1 /move_base_simple/goal geometry_msgs/PoseStamped \
           "{header:{frame_id: 'camera_init'}, pose:{position:{x: 2.0, y: 0.0, z: 1.0}, orientation:{w: 1.0}}}"
  -->

  <!-- exploration_node reads odometry_topic from d455.yaml (=/aft_mapped_to_odom)
       and subscribes globally; this top-level remap points it at FAST-LIVO2. -->
  <remap from="/aft_mapped_to_odom" to="/aft_mapped_to_init" />

  <!-- traj_server uses a PRIVATE NodeHandle ("~") and does
       getParam("odometry_topic") (traj_server.cpp:346,350). d455.yaml is
       loaded into exploration_node's private ns, so traj_server never sees
       it and subscribes to a bogus empty topic -> no /planning/pos_cmd.
       Inject the param by absolute name so traj_server gets odometry
       straight from FAST-LIVO2. -->
  <param name="/traj_server/odometry_topic" value="/aft_mapped_to_init" />

  <include file="$(find epic_planner)/launch/d455.launch" />
</launch>
